## Continuity Findings

The three artifacts assure consistent continuation because each answers a different question:

```
full guide asks:
  what does the project mean?

fold asks:
  how must it think and sound?

seed asks:
  what exists now and what should happen next?
```

Authority order should remain explicit:

```
full guide
  ↓ distilled into
fold
  ↓ current state encoded in
seed
  ↓ realized through
implementation
```

When conflict appears:

```
ethical/narrative conflict → full guide governs
tone/compression conflict  → fold governs
current implementation     → seed governs
code behavior               → repository confirms
```

---

## Required Continuity Amendments

Five small additions would complete the current handoff.

### 1. Declare the world hierarchy

Add to seed/fold:

```
site/world      :: The Observatory
expedition 001  :: A Field Guide for an Alien Learning to Listen
transmission 01 :: The Invitation to Speak
```

### 2. Refine Relay status

Current intent is not “remove Relay.”  
It is “establish its world-presence without opening live automation.”

Use:

```
relay.concept          :: established
relay.world-presence   :: permitted
relay.static-route     :: optional
relay.mail-automation  :: PARKED!
relay.ai-response      :: PARKED!
relay.open-condition   :: privacy + safety + retention + review workflow defined
```

### 3. Preserve the Nexus direction

```
future.community ::

  Observatory
    private encounter
    noticing
    reflection
    revision

  Nexus
    ephemeral traveler connection
    structured exchange
    resonance
    no permanent popularity economy

  status
    conceptual only
    implementation deferred
```

Important:

```
ephemeral != consequence-free
nothing-saved claim requires technical proof
```

### 4. Add invariant-change protocol

```
when an invariant changes:

  update full guide first
  regenerate / revise fold
  update seed current-state
  note implementation migration

never silently reinterpret
```

### 5. Add instrument threshold

```
new instrument permitted only when:
  it reveals something prose alone cannot
  OR
  it changes the reader's attention meaningfully

instrument !decoration
interaction !feature accumulation
```

